entItemId":16873,"EventItemGuid":"A41039E7-D3A0-4EA2-BA86-0A6AC97F7849","EventItemLastModifiedUtc":"2018-04-25T18:47:02.86","EventItemRowVersion":"AAAAAAAgJSI=","EventItemEventId":1130,"EventItemAgendaSequence":5,"EventItemMinutesSequence":5,"EventItemAgendaNumber":"1.","EventItemVideo":null,"EventItemVideoIndex":null,"EventItemVersion":"1","EventItemAgendaNote":null,"EventItemMinutesNote":null,"EventItemActionId":383,"EventItemActionName":"approved","EventItemActionText":"Commissioner Couchman made a motion that a recommendation be made in favor to the Board of Zoning Appeals for approval of a conditional use permit (CUP) for the continuation of live entertainment for the Bey Lounge, located at 303A Mill Street NE, in the CM, Limited Commercial zone with conditions as set forth in the 2015 and 2016 CUP’s language emphasizing noise abatement and an increase to parking lot security; the CUP being valid for 12 months.\r\nCommissioner Meren seconded the motion.  \r\n\r\nChairman Kenney asked for amendments to clarify the proposal.\r\nCommissioner Meren stated that they could be more specific to noise abatement, specifically the back of the structure and the ceiling.  \r\n\r\nAgreeing, Chairman Kenney added the following language:\r\n\r\nThat the applicant should work with their acoustic engineer along with neighbors that are immediately located behind the site to abate any noise that is permeating their home and lot as best possible.  In addition that parking lot attendants increase their due diligence in mitigating patron discussions that take place in the parking lot once customers have left the establishment.\r\n\r\nCommissioners Couchman and Meren accepted the amendment language.\r\n\r\nChairman Kenney asked for further discussion.  Commissioner McCullough agreed with Chairman Kenney’s prior comments that the applicants deserve the opportunity for one last chance to mitigate noise impacting their neighbors.  She hoped that they are successful in their efforts, stating that this will be the last CUP she is willing to extend for live entertainment if complaints do not cease.\r\n\r\nThere being no further discussion Chairman Kenney called the question.\r\n\r\n                                                                                  Motion: Couchman\r\n                                                                                 Second: Meren\r\n                                                                                      Vote: 5-1\r\nNay: Cole\r\n","EventItemPassedFlag":1,"EventItemPassedFlagName":"Pass","EventItemRollCallFlag":0,"EventItemFlagExtra":0,"EventItemTitle":"Planning Commission’s recommendation to the Board of Zoning Appeals on a conditional use permit (CUP) for the continuation of live entertainment for Bey Lounge, located at 303A Mill Street NE, in the CM, Limited Commercial zone. Application filed by Rawad Hasrouni, owner.","EventItemTally":null,"EventItemAccelaRecordId":null,"EventItemConsent":0,"EventItemMoverId":null,"EventItemMover":null,"EventItemSeconderId":null,"EventItemSeconder":null,"EventItemMatterId":2393,"EventItemMatterGuid":"CF1CBD05-FB28-4024-A47C-4F57648442AF","EventItemMatterFile":"PC17-024","EventItemMatterName":null,"EventItemMatterType":"Planning Agenda Item","EventItemMatterStatus":"Passed","EventItemMatterAttachments":[]},{"EventItemId":16874,"EventItemGuid":"0078ECF3-5E67-4598-BD23-3C8713F78701","EventItemLastModifiedUtc":"2018-04-25T19:26:26.41","EventItemRowVersion":"AAAAAAAgJf4=","EventItemEventId":1130,"EventItemAgendaSequence":6,"EventItemMinutesSequence":6,"EventItemAgendaNumber":null,"EventItemVideo":null,"EventItemVideoIndex":null,"EventItemVersion":null,"EventItemAgendaNote":null,"EventItemMinutesNote":null,"EventItemActionId":null,"EventItemActionName":null,"EventItemActionText":"Commissioner McCullough made a motion that the September 27, 2017 meeting minutes be approved as drafted.  Commissioner Cole seconded the motion.\r\n\r\n  Motion: McCullough\r\nSecond: 